Let me tell you some observations about my own games...
"The first time I do serious alchemy" depends on the
actual game. It may be as early as around where the
Quest entry is located, or not before I found the VS,
or somewhere in between. It is false that "this will
typically give me thirty or so potions", rather in a
few games it will give me that amount, in other games
it can only be five. That depends on what you got in
the game, what class you played, and how dire you
possibly need to alchemize before you can start to
optimise the amount of potions in that the process.
"The worst attribute I care about" can be much less
than 13. And for the "dunk five of those potions into
a gainer", you need a couple preconditions to be valid;
mainly you need to have the gainer potions, and you
need to have enough, and are sufficiently firm that
you can spend a few of those full healing potions for
that purpose. To sum up; your assumptions don't seem
to generally apply to my own games, but rather they
apply only to games that evolve in certain ways, and
that depends also on the played character class.

